Test harness for ares (hl64; ours, under ares' ISC licence): on meeq/ares 00ebb5bb9d (the
pin in test/run/ares-build.sh), the first of the series test/run/ares-build.sh applies.

 - cartridge/testharness.cpp (new): with ARES_TEST_HARNESS set, a PI device whose registers
   sit at 0x13fe0000-0x13fe001f, attached ahead of the cart ROM / SC64 SDRAM: CMD (+0x00:
   1 screenshot of an RDRAM framebuffer to ares-test-NNNN.ppm, 2 exit with ARG0 as the
   process status), ARG0..2, MAGIC "TEST" (+0x10; plat/n64/harness.h).
   Host-side VI shots: ARES_HOST_SCREENSHOT=1 + ARES_HOST_SHOT_EVERY_MS=<ms> dump the VI's
   framebuffer to $ARES_HOST_SHOT_DIR/ares-shot-NNNN-<tag>.ppm when it first shows a
   picture, then every <ms> of wall time (checked once per VI frame; ARES_HOST_SHOT_MAX,
   default 240), one "[ares] screenshot <path> (...)" line each (test/run/menu.sh, play.sh).
 - cartridge/isviewer.cpp: with the harness the ISViewer log goes to stdout.
 - controller/gamepad/gamepad.cpp: ARES_TEST_INPUT=<file> ("<buttons-hex> <x> <y>", the
   controller word's bits) is merged into controller reads; each new press logs
   "TESTHARNESS inject ...".
 - vi/vi.cpp: the per-frame hook of the host shots.

